WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. 
(Take whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! 
Are gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.010
Looks like they finally 
found this place, too.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.030
Yeah.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:10.400
We've received a magic communique from 
our strategic reconnaissance unit.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.480
They say they've found the Scrapped 
Princess' party near the mountains.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:16.860
Only two days remain until 
the day of prophecy...

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.410
In order to appease the wrath of God,

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.950
we'll do whatever it takes to 
eliminate the Scrapped Princess.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.910
Have all Colossus units 
converge on the mountains.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:38.380
"Oratorio of the Mortals"

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:46.100
Call for a jihad if you like,

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:50.690
but we want a more certain means of 
eliminating the Providence Breaker.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.690
This is your last opportunity.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.330
We will use an emissary.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:06.470
Chris?

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:10.040
Forgive me for startling you, Highness.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:11.520
That's all right.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.640
How is my sister?

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.630
It was your team, wasn't it?

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.970
The ones that they say smuggled the 
Scrapped Princess out of the castle.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.660
I can't bring myself to believe 
that she will destroy the world.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.440
I see...

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.980
So, you've come all this way to say goodbye.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.490
Take care, Highness.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.960
Boy, you old folks are 
early risers, aren't you?

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:13.250
Shut up.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.140
It sure is pretty, isn't it?

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.460
I suppose it is.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:39.000
When I turn 16 tomorrow,

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.810
do you think the sun will 
come up just like always?

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:48.060
When the sun comes up tomorrow,

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.100
I wonder what will happen to me.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.650
Beats me.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:54.220
You'll probably make a lousy breakfast.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:01.390
It's hard to believe, isn't it?

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:06.160
I might cause trouble for 
everybody in the world.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.120
Even so...

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:13.080
Even so, I don't want to die.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.280
Is that selfish of me?

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.620
Wanting to live is selfish?

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:22.050
That's the stupidest thing I've ever heard.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.950
Even if that person was a criminal?

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:29.430
Even if lots of people died because of it?

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:30.510
I'd forgive them.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.440
Pacifica, Shannon!

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:44.790
Breakfast is ready!

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:46.780
Coming!

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:47.910
C'mon, Shannon! Let's go eat!

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:49.410
C'mon!

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:53.800
Hey!

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:03.290
Did you sleep well last night, Highness?

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.510
Yes. That is good.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:11.390
I was worried that the cries of the 
injured might have kept you awake.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:12.930
The injured?

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.680
There has been a steady stream

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:17.810
of people who were injured in 
the calamity at the capital,

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:21.150
so we have been using part of the 
temple as a makeshift hospital.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.550
If it is not too much trouble,

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:26.610
perhaps Your Highness might go visit them?

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:38.700
They come here because they have 
no money for medical treatment.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.960
Those who have survived this 
long will heal eventually.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:46.920
However...

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:51.220
There are a great many who 
have lost their lives.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:55.390
As long as the Scrapped Princess 
remains in this world,

00:06:55.390 --> 00:07:00.230
there will be more and more who 
will be injured by God's wrath.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:04.230
Highness... Please act as an emissary.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:09.280
Act as God's messenger in 
order to save your people.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.200
Whatcha grinning about?

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.830
Uh... This and that.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.290
Like what and what?

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:21.290
It's Chris... He said, "Thank you."

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:22.670
When I gave him his breakfast.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.800
And what are <i>you </i>grinning about?

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:28.380
Hey, you two!

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:30.980
The Royal Forces are closing in!

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.630
Get your butts back to camp!

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:34.090
Yeah, so?

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:34.890
Now look here, kid...

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:38.850
Besides, doing the laundry 
is all I'm good for.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:47.400
Maybe that's your own way of fighting.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.470
What's that mean?

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.710
It's something Eirote told me.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:54.490
She said everybody has 
her own way of fighting.

00:07:56.530 --> 00:08:00.790
My whole life, I've wanted 
to change the world.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:05.580
I said I'd smash this rotten world to pieces.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:06.750
But...

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:09.550
It's not perfect by a long shot,

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:13.220
but maybe this world isn't so bad.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.680
When this is over, take me to your village.

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:21.140
Sure, you're welcome to come by.

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:22.310
I'll come, too!

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.630
Sure, sure! C'mon over!

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:26.190
I'll cook you a huge feast!

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:28.400
That's okay, I'll do the cooking.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.650
That's so mean!

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:42.580
Hey, those are supposed to be 
finely sliced! Cut 'em thinner!

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:43.710
Oh. Right.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:45.540
You're such a nitpicker, Shannon.

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:47.650
Mr. Berkens?!

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:52.210
Hi, mister! It's good to see you!

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.680
Good to see you, too, little lady.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:57.890
He says that he has a message. 
What should we do with him?

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:00.820
He's okay. So, what's the message?

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:04.600
Prince Forsyth says that he 
wants to meet the little lady.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:06.350
Prince Forsyth? Who's that?

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:08.810
Your older brother.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.430
But why the sudden interest in meeting her?

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:19.120
Apparently, he wants to meet his little 
sister just once before her birthday.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.620
What's your answer?

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:24.580
My answer?

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:28.610
How am I supposed to react 
to that at a time like this?

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.800
I'm the Scrapped Princess, remember?

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:37.010
He's the prince of a country that's 
trying its hardest to kill me.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.090
You might say he's my brother,

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:41.780
but it's not like I've even met him.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:44.430
I wonder why he wants to 
meet now, of all times...

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:48.790
What kind of guy is this prince?

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:51.170
If he were king,

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:53.400
I doubt he would go to 
war without good reason.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:57.020
The prince has been concerned about 
you for as long as I've known him.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.370
Perhaps he wants to meet 
you and see for himself.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:04.880
See if you really are the poison 
that will destroy the world.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:09.210
I'm supposed return to the 
holy city with your answer.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:12.250
If you're going to meet him, 
we'll need to make arrangements.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:13.920
Otherwise, I'll just head back.

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:16.130
Think it over until this evening,

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:17.730
and then give me your answer.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:40.610
What is it?

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:46.330
Nothing, I was just thinking about 
how life is full of troubles.

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:51.710
Oh, right, you were agonizing over 
what chivalry is that one time.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:52.700
Yes...

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.340
Did you figure it out?

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.670
No, not yet...

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:57.650
Oh.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:01.680
I always thought that there 
had to be a right and wrong

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.640
that everyone could believe in.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:09.640
But now I think that maybe 
there's no such thing.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:16.110
If I believed in what the kingdom and 
the Church of Mauser say is right,

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:19.570
then that wouldn't be what is 
right from your point of view.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:24.120
Because of that, I no longer knew 
what was right and what was wrong,

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:26.280
but then I realized something.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:31.060
I realized that all I really 
wanted to do was protect you.

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:38.240
But enough about me.

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:41.880
I had hoped that I could 
help you with your problems.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.720
You wanted to give <i>me </i>advice?

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:47.400
Well, I don't think I would be 
of much help, but I still...

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:49.850
No, of course you would.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:51.350
You really mean that?!

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:52.800
When I talk to you, Leo,

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:55.650
worrying about things seems 
stupid all of a sudden.

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:58.150
Really? It does? I'm so glad to hear that!

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:04.110
It's too bad my big brother 
isn't a good person like you...

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:06.270
I'm sure that he is.

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:10.580
Once he meets you, I'm sure he'll like you!

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:12.330
You think so?

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.580
All right, I'll decide for you.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:15.210
We'll go meet him.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:18.170
We only go around once in life, after all.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:20.930
Even if you fail spectacularly,

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:23.630
isn't it better to try and fail 
than to regret not trying at all?

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:28.640
You never change, do you, Leo?

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:30.780
I'm sorry...

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.930
That headband...

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:34.020
Yes?

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:38.150
That isn't the one that I tied around 
your head back when we first met, is it?

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:39.610
Um... Yes.

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:41.970
You should wash that thing.

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:43.570
I will. I'm sorry.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:46.450
Leo.

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:47.530
Yes?

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:49.990
Thanks a lot.

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.920
They're just barely inside firing range.

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:01.670
I wonder if they'll launch 
a full offensive at dawn.

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:04.170
Once the sun sets, we 
should make our move, too.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:10.100
Here.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:13.530
Thank you.

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:15.560
Um, listen...

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:17.430
What is it?

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:20.610
Pacifica...

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:28.990
Pacifica didn't remember the man 
she met while she had amnesia.

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:34.130
Pacifica didn't come out 
and say it or anything,

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:37.000
but I think that she really cared for him.

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:41.550
She cared for him, but 
she doesn't remember him.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:42.510
Nothing at all.

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:47.510
But you remember that person, don't you?

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:54.380
I heard once that people are creatures 
who forget the painful things.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.480
That they can go on living 
because they forget.

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:03.650
I'm sorry for how I acted in the capital.

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:05.200
Ignoring you, I mean.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:10.910
I didn't want to get you involved in 
all this Scrapped Princess business.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.060
It's okay.

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:17.370
It's all okay now.

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:24.910
What's the matter?

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:27.670
Leo said something to me once.

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:31.800
That she's got a nobility to her 
that you can't find in commoners.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:34.630
It's no surprise, I guess.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:38.270
After all, she's not a commoner.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.490
Did you want her to say that 
she wouldn't go meet him?

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:46.030
If she says that she wants 
to go see her real brother,

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.740
I've got no right to stop her.

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:51.740
Say, Shannon...

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:55.360
What's a "real" brother, anyway?

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:59.330
Who's your little sister?

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.500
Is anything going to change?

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:04.980
I guess not.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:08.720
Shannon! Raquel!

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:13.680
Um, listen...

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:16.770
I wanna go meet him.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:20.120
I want to go meet this guy 
they say is my twin brother.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.730
Sure. Go see him.

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:31.830
Shall we go?

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:33.820
Prince Forsyth?

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:35.800
Is something the matter?

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:37.270
No.

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.420
Don't mind me.

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:54.820
I just wanted a breath of fresh air.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:56.070
Yes, sir.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:57.810
What's that?

00:15:57.810 --> 00:16:00.140
Something my wife gave to me when I left.

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:04.650
She said to sow them after I came back.

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:08.310
They're seeds of yellow 
violets, her favorite flower.

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:11.420
I see you found yourself a fine wife.

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:13.070
And you, General?

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:17.160
I haven't been able to find 
someone to spend my days with.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:19.620
I ended up being married to this.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:24.080
Excuse me, sir.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:26.760
Message from the holy city.

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:29.050
As expected, target has changed.

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:33.010
Good. We begin our attack at sunset.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:40.430
Zefiris?

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:42.090
You're going, then?

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:45.040
It will be midnight in a few hours.

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:46.940
Be careful.

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:47.480
Sure.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:51.440
I'll be praying that nothing bad happens.

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:54.150
Thanks.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:57.970
Um, I...

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:00.050
You must be Pacifica.

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:02.640
Uh... Yes. Nice to meet you.

00:18:03.310 --> 00:18:06.680
So, um...

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:08.290
Uh...

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:11.770
What's your favorite food?

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:15.940
I like eggs! Er, egg dishes!

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:17.820
Especially omelets!

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.700
I love eggs, too.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:24.380
I knew it! Maybe it's 
because we're twins, huh?

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:28.960
I'm sorry.

00:18:33.470 --> 00:18:38.220
I'm sorry for all of the hardships 
that I put you through.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.380
No, no, it's not your fault!

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:44.560
In all the time that you were being 
hunted down as the Scrapped Princess,

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:47.850
I couldn't do anything to help you.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:50.800
Big brother...

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:54.230
Don't worry about it.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:56.630
Some parts of my life were rough,

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:58.820
but not everything.

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:07.020
That's my big brother and my big sister,

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:08.750
along with our friends.

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:12.670
They seem like nice people.

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:13.550
They are.

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:21.180
I'm sorry...

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:27.640
I truly am sorry.

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:31.100
I finally met you, but I...

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:55.970
Prince Forsyth!

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:12.230
Hey! They're aiming at the church!

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:13.650
They wouldn't!

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:16.150
I don't get it! The prince is in there!

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:18.260
Pacifica?

00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:19.610
Pacifica?

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:21.570
Pacifica?!

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:28.140
Pacifica...

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:32.620
Shannon. I might be able 
to do something for her

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:34.500
with my phase interference capabilities.

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:36.650
It might take a while, though.

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:39.920
I won't allow you to interfere.

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:46.470
B-Barrier... Barrier, protect us!

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:53.570
I didn't expect him to go this far.

00:20:53.570 --> 00:20:55.400
This is an unexpected bonus.

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:57.560
Shannon Cassul.

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:01.530
You and the Dragoon will come with me.

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:04.820
If you refuse, I will burn the 
capital to the ground right now.

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:08.780
Shannon...

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:16.250
Raquel...

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:19.220
Take care of Pacifica.

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:29.030
Zefiris.

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:44.530
God's messenger has appeared?

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:46.490
Step up the bombardment!

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:49.450
Prepare to launch!

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:52.410
How...

00:21:52.960 --> 00:21:55.120
How could this have happened?

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:01.040
Prince Forsyth... Why?

00:22:01.860 --> 00:22:03.450
Please forgive me...

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:08.660
As their prince, I had 
to protect my people...

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:13.510
I at least wanted to die with my sister...

00:22:17.690 --> 00:22:18.900
Pacifica?

00:22:41.580 --> 00:22:46.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:22:46.730 --> 00:22:52.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:22:52.050 --> 00:22:59.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:22:59.230 --> 00:23:05.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:10.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:23:10.150 --> 00:23:13.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:18.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:23:18.370 --> 00:23:24.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:28.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:31.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:38.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:23:38.220 --> 00:23:40.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:23:40.180 --> 00:23:44.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets sail. 
(The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:50.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:23:50.190 --> 00:23:53.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:23:53.530 --> 00:23:57.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:23:58.490 --> 00:24:11.470
"Next Time"

00:23:59.460 --> 00:24:01.290
Pacifica has been stabbed by her brother.

00:24:01.290 --> 00:24:04.000
Though her sister lies bleeding before 
her, Raquel can do nothing to save her.

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:05.710
And Shannon, who was threatened that the 
capital would be burned to the ground,

00:24:05.710 --> 00:24:09.010
is forced to fuse with Zefiris, and 
he goes to fight the Peacemakers.

00:24:09.010 --> 00:24:11.470
There are now only 14 words 
left in this final preview!

00:24:11.470 --> 00:24:13.170
Next time, the finale of <i>Scrapped Princess</i>!

00:24:13.170 --> 00:24:14.540
"Symphony of the Protectors."

00:24:14.540 --> 00:24:15.470
Please tune in!
